WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.069 --> 00:00:05.690
Star Wars: The Last Jedi just dropped a chilling
but thrilling teaser trailer that hints at

00:00:05.690 --> 00:00:09.080
some awesome scenes in the second instalment
of the new trilogy.

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:13.009
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here
and in this video, I'm breaking down The Last

00:00:13.009 --> 00:00:17.060
Jedi teaser and explaining some intriguing
details you might have missed.

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:21.391
Just be aware I'll be discussing speculation
and possible spoilers for Star Wars: The Last

00:00:21.391 --> 00:00:25.529
Jedi, so if you want to avoid those, tap in
the top-right of the screen for a spoiler-free

00:00:25.529 --> 00:00:29.589
video tribute to Carrie Fisher at Star Wars
Celebration.

00:00:29.589 --> 00:00:33.090
Starting with that first scene, I thought
it was interesting that there's a little parallel

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:37.420
to the start of The Force Awakens trailer
where Finn popped up in distress while here

00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:42.800
Rey also appears distressed and I wonder whether
she's just experienced another force vision,

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:47.090
like she did when she picked up Luke's lightsaber
for the first time in The Force Awakens.

00:00:47.090 --> 00:00:52.300
And that dark area in the rocks just behind
Rey feels like it could be the same cave entrance

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:54.879
we see Luke standing in at the end of the
trailer.

00:00:54.879 --> 00:00:59.710
And if you brighten the image here, the walls
of the cave actually look like part of a tree

00:00:59.710 --> 00:01:03.420
and you can also make out what looks like
Rey's staff by the entrance.

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:08.000
The idea of a cave also harkens back to the
Dark Side Cave that Luke entered in The Empire

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:12.720
Strikes Back where he struck down a vision
of Darth Vader revealing his own face beneath

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:13.720
Vader's mask.

00:01:13.720 --> 00:01:14.720
What I also find fascinating is that the visuals
in this opening shot immediately introduce

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:15.720
us to the theme of light and darkness in the
new movie.

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:16.720
Notice how the image starts with what looks
like stars in a night sky or space, but then

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:17.720
light illuminates the scene revealing the
stars as just specks or shiny flecks on the

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:18.720
rock.

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:19.720
So, getting in to the core of the trailer,
after the Lucasfilm logo appears, we get some

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:22.320
beautiful shots of Ahch'To, the location where
Rey discovered Luke at the end of The Force

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:23.340
Awakens.

00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:28.759
We next get the first of various voices starting
with Luke saying "Breathe", "just breathe"

00:01:28.759 --> 00:01:31.100
and then "reach out, what do you see?"

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:34.570
The last words echo back to Yoda who says
"Reach out.

00:01:34.570 --> 00:01:38.950
Sense the Force around you" while training
Jedi Younglings in Episode 2: Attack of the

00:01:38.950 --> 00:01:39.950
Clones.

00:01:39.950 --> 00:01:43.909
And the repeating of the word 'breath' fits
in with the way Yoda and Obi-Wan, for example,

00:01:43.909 --> 00:01:48.990
emphasised the importance of calmness, concentration,
and mindfulness when it came to the Force.

00:01:48.990 --> 00:01:52.830
And in the background there are whispers of
"Help me, Obi-Wan" just as the trailer cuts

00:01:52.830 --> 00:01:57.840
to Leia examining a star chart, then on the
shot of Kylo Ren's destroyed mask you can

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:03.219
hear Darth Vader breathing in the background,
then the words "seduced by the dark side"

00:02:03.219 --> 00:02:08.149
which Obi-Wan says when he appears as a Force
Ghost to Luke in Return of the Jedi.

00:02:08.149 --> 00:02:13.190
Next we hear Yoda whisper "surrounds us and
binds us" the words he said to Luke while

00:02:13.190 --> 00:02:16.170
training him in The Empire Strikes Back.

00:02:16.170 --> 00:02:20.300
Hearing other voices in the background makes
me think we could well get Force Ghosts of

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:24.660
Obi-Wan, Yoda or Anakin Skywalker appearing
in The Last Jedi.

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:29.000
Or these could just be disembodied voices
again like the ones Rey heard during her vision

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:30.270
in The Force Awakens.

00:02:30.270 --> 00:02:32.800
Now, jumping back to the visuals in the trailer.

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:37.040
I really love this shot of Rey's hand and
little stones rising up around her, which

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:41.390
is reminiscent of of Luke levitating objects
when he trained with Yoda on Dagobah, and

00:02:41.390 --> 00:02:44.050
also reminded me a touch of Man of Steel as
well.

00:02:44.050 --> 00:02:48.370
By the way, I think it's curious that two
of these images of Rey focus on her hand and

00:02:48.370 --> 00:02:51.650
I wonder whether the teaser is hinting at
something more here.

00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:55.710
After all the opening scene to The Force Awakens
was initially going to be Luke Skywalker's

00:02:55.710 --> 00:03:00.470
severed hand with his lightsaber from the
end of The Empire Strikes Back floating through

00:03:00.470 --> 00:03:01.470
space.

00:03:01.470 --> 00:03:04.560
Next in the trailer we get this intriguing
shot of a series of books set against some

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:05.600
tree roots.

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:09.770
On the page of one of the books is the insignia
of the Jedi Order and these are probably the

00:03:09.770 --> 00:03:11.840
legendary Journal of the Whills.

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:16.230
The Whills were recently mentioned in Rogue
One via Chirrut Imwe and Baze Malbus who were

00:03:16.230 --> 00:03:17.820
Guardians of the Whills.

00:03:17.820 --> 00:03:21.621
The Whills was George Lucas's original term
for The Force when he was writing the first

00:03:21.621 --> 00:03:22.630
Star Wars movie.

00:03:22.630 --> 00:03:27.480
I think it's very likely we'll see the term
and concept developed in The Last Jedi.

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:31.960
As for those tree roots Force-sensitive trees
have appeared outside the movies in Star Wars

00:03:31.960 --> 00:03:36.590
canon like The Clone Wars animated series
and the Shattered Empire comic book series.

00:03:36.590 --> 00:03:40.960
In The Clone Wars, there was a force-sensitive
tree in the Jedi Temple on Coruscant and we

00:03:40.960 --> 00:03:45.370
know from Han Solo in The Force Awakens that
Luke likely disappeared to look for the first

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:46.370
Jedi Temple.

00:03:46.370 --> 00:03:51.320
If he did indeed find that first Jedi Temple
on Ahch'To, then it seems quite likely these

00:03:51.320 --> 00:03:52.990
are the fabled Journal of the Whills.

00:03:52.990 --> 00:03:58.540
By the way, I also love how the imagery of
Rey's words lines up with the images on screen.

00:03:58.540 --> 00:04:03.310
When she says "Light" we get Leia, she says
"Darkness" and we see Kylo Ren's destroyed

00:04:03.310 --> 00:04:08.240
mask and the word "Balance" brings us to the
Jedi books with a ray of light illuminating

00:04:08.240 --> 00:04:09.580
the darkness.

00:04:09.580 --> 00:04:13.610
And these words also mirror the poem in the
Journal of the Whills which reads:

00:04:13.610 --> 00:04:16.480
"First comes the day
Then comes the night.

00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:19.550
After the darkness
Shines through the light."

00:04:19.550 --> 00:04:24.560
But after all that perfect symmetry, comes
the kicker with Luke's words, "it's so much

00:04:24.560 --> 00:04:28.320
bigger", suggesting that there's much more
to it than this, and I'll come back to that

00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:29.320
later.

00:04:29.320 --> 00:04:32.960
The trailer then breaks into some really fantastic
action scenes.

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:37.330
First up are these Resistance fighters squaring
up to the new First Order Heavy Assault Walkers

00:04:37.330 --> 00:04:41.440
in the distance which, although we can't see
them up close here, are getting on for twice

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:45.720
the size of a regular AT-AT and have also
been dubbed "Gorilla Walkers" because of their

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:46.890
enormous thick legs.

00:04:46.890 --> 00:04:51.380
Now, if you're wondering why those fighters
are giving off a red flare, well, the important

00:04:51.380 --> 00:04:56.040
thing to think about is that this battle is
taking place on the planet Crait, which director

00:04:56.040 --> 00:05:00.240
Rian Johnson has said is 'a mineral planet'
covered in salt that's home to an abandoned

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:01.410
rebel base.

00:05:01.410 --> 00:05:05.820
If you notice this figher's craft, it seems
to be hitting the salt floor and piercing

00:05:05.820 --> 00:05:08.120
it, which spews out red dust.

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:12.590
And notice how all the fighters have a kind
of spike dragging along the salt floor which

00:05:12.590 --> 00:05:14.670
is where the red is spewing from.

00:05:14.670 --> 00:05:18.850
The planet they're on has a red-coloured mineral
base under the salt, so it looks like they're

00:05:18.850 --> 00:05:22.990
trying to break up the ground before they
reach the First Order walkers to create a

00:05:22.990 --> 00:05:26.950
smokescreen so the walkers can't see properly
during their attack.

00:05:26.950 --> 00:05:31.210
Obviously, this scene calls back to the Rebel
attack on the Imperial walkers on the snowy

00:05:31.210 --> 00:05:35.980
planet Hoth in The Empire Strikes Back, and
the visuals here are absolutely breathtaking.

00:05:35.980 --> 00:05:40.580
By the way, this battle scene was filmed on
real salt flats in Bolivia.

00:05:40.580 --> 00:05:44.980
It's nice to see Finn is getting medical attention
here and there a little of the Aurebesh language

00:05:44.980 --> 00:05:49.870
showing on Finn's pod which translates as
"Stable", indicating that we're likely to

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:52.540
see Finn back in action in The Last Jedi.

00:05:52.540 --> 00:05:57.150
The trailer gives us a very short glimpse
of Kylo Ren and interestingly, his scar here

00:05:57.150 --> 00:06:00.630
looks different from how Rey scared him at
the end of The Force Awakens

00:06:00.630 --> 00:06:04.790
But what's more intriguing is the bright yellow
light behind him because the website Making

00:06:04.790 --> 00:06:09.000
Star Wars has reported there's a scene in
The Last Jedi where the Force tree on Ahch'To

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:10.290
is set on fire.

00:06:10.290 --> 00:06:14.520
We know from The Force Awakens that Kylo Ren
was obsessed with finding where Luke Skywalker

00:06:14.520 --> 00:06:19.160
had disappeared to, and I wonder whether Kylo's
found Luke and set the tree on fire.

00:06:19.160 --> 00:06:22.750
And it looks like here, we've got another
look at that scene which appeared in Rey's

00:06:22.750 --> 00:06:27.680
force vision of Luke and R2-D2 watching what
might be his Jedi training school burn down.

00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:31.590
Hopefully, we'll get a more in-depth look
at what happened to Luke and R2-D2 and how

00:06:31.590 --> 00:06:34.090
his hand ended up like this.

00:06:34.090 --> 00:06:37.850
And the way the trailer cuts to a scene of
Phasma and Stormtroopers walking through an

00:06:37.850 --> 00:06:43.230
area that's on fire is meant to suggest that
Phasma was there when Luke's school was destroyed,

00:06:43.230 --> 00:06:47.840
but actually notice the floor she's walking
on is shiny and if you look up, it looks like

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:52.030
this may be more like the place where Poe
Dameron's X-wing is blown up earlier in the

00:06:52.030 --> 00:06:53.389
trailer.

00:06:53.389 --> 00:06:57.630
By the way, assuming this isn't a flashback
scene for Phasma, I guess she managed to escape

00:06:57.630 --> 00:07:01.471
the trash compactor on Starkiller Base where
Finn and friends said they'd dump her in The

00:07:01.471 --> 00:07:02.590
Force Awakens!

00:07:02.590 --> 00:07:07.600
Ok, and then the trailer ends with those chilling
words of Luke's, "It's time for the Jedi to

00:07:07.600 --> 00:07:08.600
end."

00:07:08.600 --> 00:07:12.540
Now, it's a bit shocking after 8 movies to
think that Star Wars might be trying to do

00:07:12.540 --> 00:07:15.500
away with the Jedi, but Luke may actually
have a point.

00:07:15.500 --> 00:07:19.340
He's had two of his relatives turn away from
the Jedi to the Dark Side of the Force.

00:07:19.340 --> 00:07:23.470
So, perhaps, he thinks there is a better way
to wield the power of the Force, even combining

00:07:23.470 --> 00:07:27.240
both the Light and Dark sides in what some
fans call the Grey Jedi.

00:07:27.240 --> 00:07:31.030
And, in fact, the second part of the poem
I mentioned earlier from the Journal of the

00:07:31.030 --> 00:07:33.210
Whills reads:
"The difference, they say,

00:07:33.210 --> 00:07:35.860
Is only made right
By the resolving of gray

00:07:35.860 --> 00:07:37.880
Through refined Jedi sight."

00:07:37.880 --> 00:07:43.550
So, could the idea be that a grey Force user
is going to replace the old Jedi, hence the

00:07:43.550 --> 00:07:45.560
title of the movie "The Last Jedi"?

00:07:45.560 --> 00:07:50.680
By the way, the poster for The Last Jedi also
seems to be hinting at a possible blurring

00:07:50.680 --> 00:07:55.610
of the Light Side and the Dark Side as notice
that Rey's lightsaber begins blue and then

00:07:55.610 --> 00:07:58.170
changes to red further up the poster.

00:07:58.170 --> 00:08:01.540
So, guys, what did you think of The Last Jedi
teaser trailer?

00:08:01.540 --> 00:08:04.449
And what did you make of Luke's final words?

00:08:04.449 --> 00:08:06.610
And did you spot anything else I missed?

00:08:06.610 --> 00:08:09.169
I'd love to hear your thoughts in the comments
below.

00:08:09.169 --> 00:08:12.730
If you enjoyed this, I really appreciate your
likes and shares, and check out some of my

00:08:12.730 --> 00:08:16.620
other trailer breakdowns and Star Wars videos
by tapping or clicking here.

00:08:16.620 --> 00:08:18.700
Thanks for watching and see ya next time!

00:08:18.700 --> 00:08:19.090
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers!

